WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.150
No heroic saga is complete without a villain.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:08.260
The MCU has suffered no lack of baddies thus
far, and Phase Four promises to continue that

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:09.260
trend.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:14.019
Today, we're taking a look at every new villain
coming our way in Phase Four of the MCU.

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:18.580
One of the few Phase Four villains we've gotten
a decent glimpse of is Black Widow's Taskmaster,

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.080
AKA Anthony Masters.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.930
As a boy, Masters discovered that he could
replicate any physical action once he has

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:24.930
observed it.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.530
Empowered by these "photographic reflexes,"
Taskmaster turns to a life of crime and becomes

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:30.830
extremely wealthy.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.960
Looking to expand his reach, he opens a school
where he shapes other villains into lean,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.680
mean, good-guy-busting machines.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.790
Since he's able to replicate the fighting
style of any hero, he provides his pupils

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.390
with uniquely individualized training.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.700
Taskmaster's abilities prove enormously dangerous
in the heat of battle, as he can predict his

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.090
foes' next moves and stay several steps ahead.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:54.540
He should prove an interesting foe for Natasha
in Black Widow, given her own skills with

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.260
subterfuge adaptation.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.880
Admittedly, fans have sort of encountered
the Mandarin already.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.810
Marvel pulled the rug out from underneath
us in Iron Man 3 by portraying Ben Kingsley

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.530
as the classic villain, only to reveal him
as an actor named Trevor Slattery.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.310
He was only ever hired to portray a made-up
supervillain.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.820
That wasn't the end for the Mandarin, however.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.830
Fans will be getting the real deal in Shang-Chi
and the Legend of the Ten Rings, with Tony

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:20.290
Leung Chiu-wai set to portray the actual,
no-fooling Mandarin.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:24.979
The Mandarin is both intellectually and physically
formidable, but the biggest threat he poses

00:01:24.979 --> 00:01:26.840
comes from the ten rings he wears.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.620
Crafted from the remains of a crashed alien
spaceship, each ring grants him a different

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:31.620
ability.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.220
How Shang-Chi will handle such a formidable
threat remains to be seen, but it's certain

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.659
to be an unmissable showdown.

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:41.970
Eternals was a bit of a surprise announcement
- they're not exactly a high-profile super-team.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.240
Then again, Guardians of the Galaxy was a
massive success, and Iron Man used to be a

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:49.340
C-list hero before becoming the MCU's poster
boy.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.870
Why shouldn't a race of immortal, cosmic beings
with fabulous taste in leotards become Marvel's

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:54.870
next big thing?

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.620
Who will menace the titular Eternals?

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:57.620
The Deviants.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.560
Genetic offshoots of the Eternals, they were
driven into hiding after an attempted rebellion

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.950
against the Celestials, the godlike alien
creators of both groups.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.840
We're not yet sure which specific characters
will be villains in Eternals - many Deviants

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.380
have come and gone over the years.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:14.870
Regardless of who ends up in the film, though,
we're sure to be in for a wild ride.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:18.760
Doctor Strange and the Multiverse of Madness
will allegedly take the MCU into the realm

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.760
of horror.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:23.700
All signs point to one of the central villains
of the film being Nightmare, a powerful demon

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.980
who has been one of Doctor Strange's most
prominent foes for decades.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.010
Nightmare is extraordinarily powerful.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:32.661
He controls a terrifying part of the Dream
Dimension called the Nightmare World, where

00:02:32.661 --> 00:02:34.680
he feeds off human psychic energy.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:39.230
He can completely incapacitate powerful heroes,
and even use his influence to dominate and

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.379
control others.

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:44.459
Not only would he be a formidable foe for
Doctor Strange, it's easy to imagine him stepping

00:02:44.459 --> 00:02:48.030
into an ongoing antagonist role, similar to
Loki.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.980
We know that Druig will be part of The Eternals,
and that Barry Keoghan is stepping into the

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:52.980
role.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.490
We also know that Druig will likely be a villain,
as he is one of the group's classic foes.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:00.990
However, we're still calling it a rumor because
we know so little about Eternals at this time.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.300
If Druig does wind up being a villain, he
will be a formidable one.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.240
Druig is not actually a Deviant, but an Eternal,
long-lived and enormously powerful.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:13.890
His abilities are vast and varied: telekinesis,
flight, telepathy, matter transformation,

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.500
and illusion are all within his wheelhouse.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.490
On top of that, he is a ruthless, highly intelligent
schemer, and the ruler of an entire country

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:21.830
in the comics.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:26.519
The MCU will be expanding to include Disney+
television shows in phase 4, and the first

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:29.349
show to see release will be The Falcon and
the Winter Soldier.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:33.180
We know that Zemo will be a central villain
of that series, but he might not be alone:

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.330
John Walker, aka U.S. Agent, might just join
him.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:41.550
Walker was created in the 1980s to serve as
a dark reflection of Captain America's idealism.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.769
Where Captain America personifies all the
positive traits of being American, U.S. Agent

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:50.990
is patriotism taken to ugly, violent extremes
of nationalism, xenophobia, and callousness.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:55.299
Though Walker has changed his ways over the
years, ending up a good guy, he certainly

00:03:55.299 --> 00:03:58.909
didn't debut that way, and seems likely to
serve as one of The Falcon and the Winter

00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:01.030
Soldier's electrifying villains.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:05.349
Thor: Love and Thunder is now slated for a
February 2022 release.

00:04:05.349 --> 00:04:07.930
Standing in Thor's way will be... someone.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.260
We don't yet know the character, but we do
know the villain will be played by Christian

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.260
Bale.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.590
Most of the evidence indicates that Bale will
play Gorr, the God Butcher.

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.019
Gorr is an alien from an impoverished planet.

00:04:18.019 --> 00:04:21.539
After losing his loved ones, he arrives at
the conclusion that there are no gods.

00:04:21.539 --> 00:04:24.439
He is shocked, then, to discover that gods
are entirely real.

00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:26.809
They just did nothing as he and his family
starved.

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:30.539
From that day on, he makes it his goal to
destroy as many gods as he can find.

00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:32.409
Gorr would be a great foe for Thor.

00:04:32.409 --> 00:04:37.309
His weapon, All-Black the Necrosword, is arguably
more powerful than Mjolnir, and his backstory

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:38.569
is enormously compelling.

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:44.050
In an era of the MCU bursting with Eternals,
Sorcerers Supreme, and Asgardian gods, throwing

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.500
a nonbeliever like Gorr into the mix could
make for an incredible movie.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:48.500
"I don't know.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:49.500
I never knew.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.710
I swear to God, man."

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.710
"SWEAR TO ME!"

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:56.160
The Loki Disney+ series will most likely follow
the rogue timeline Loki created by stealing

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.099
the Tesseract in Avengers: Endgame.

00:04:58.099 --> 00:05:02.349
However, some small details hint at who Loki
will be up against in that series: the Time

00:05:02.349 --> 00:05:03.460
Variance Authority.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:08.190
The TVA is essentially a group of time-traveling
police who seek to stop those who would screw

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.809
up the multiverse's timeline.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:14.499
The Loki spot revealed during the Super Bowl
showed Loki as a prisoner of the TVA, so we

00:05:14.499 --> 00:05:16.649
know they'll at least be a part of the series.

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.440
This brings us to Owen Wilson.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.229
Wilson has been cast as an unknown role in
Loki, and the rumor mill has pegged him as

00:05:22.229 --> 00:05:23.229
Justice Peace.

00:05:23.229 --> 00:05:27.259
Though Peace takes himself very seriously,
he is often played for laughs.

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:31.210
Wilson's comedic experience, paired with Hiddleston's
charm, could work perfectly.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.889
"Staying nimble.

00:05:32.889 --> 00:05:36.210
Till I get the call from the mothership.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:38.029
My raison d'etre.

00:05:38.029 --> 00:05:39.499
Then I'll fight."

